  "description": "Why this pullback is a shakeout, not a top, and how I am positioning for the next leg higher",
  "body_html": "<p>Feeling bored? Or unmotivated? You are not alone. For the last month, investors have been whiplashed out of the market. Strong swings up and down…mostly down…have exhausted a wide range of traders. </p><h4><strong>Do not leave!</strong></h4><p>There is no indication that the bull market is over. I wish stocks went up every single day…how glorious it would be! But you have to stick around during the hard times to take part in the good times. That doesn’t mean throw your money everywhere and hope for the best. But check in once a day, or every other day. I don’t send out buy signals every day…but when I do, its because the<em><strong> market is working for us.</strong></em> We double down or even triple down during those periods of time. </p><p>Do I think we have a “forever” bull market ahead of us? No. </p><p>Do I think we have another, massive, euphoric, bullish leg ahead of us? Yes!</p><h4>Why the bull market remains intact</h4><p>Everything in this article: <em><strong><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/leaders-forming-under-the-surface?r=4z8lgl\">Stock Market Leaders Forming Under the Surface</a></strong></em> remains true today. The VIX has been chopping upwards…but no breakouts and no higher highs. The Russell 2000 still appears significantly stronger than the S&amp;P 500. And we are still seeing more stocks make 52 week highs than 52 week lows.<a class=\"footnote-anchor\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteAnchorToDOM\" id=\"footnote-anchor-1\" href=\"#footnote-1\" target=\"_self\">1</a></p><p>Sentiment is pretty low…normal after a month long of downwards chop. However, nothing has truly crashed. There were hoards of investors into Novo Nordisk, Paypal, Netflix, all of which have went down significantly more, driving sentiment even further down. However…these stocks have been in a steady down trend. This is just “buy the dip” individuals being punished for a bad habit. Of course they are pissed.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!bS3e!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcd921205-081e-4f13-b590-b3e3b03242bf_1309x812.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!bS3e!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcd921205-081e-4f13-b590-b3e3b03242bf_1309x812.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!bS3e!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcd921205-081e-4f13-b590-b3e3b03242bf_1309x812.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!bS3e!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcd921205-081e-4f13-b590-b3e3b03242bf_1309x812.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!bS3e!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcd921205-081e-4f13-b590-b3e3b03242bf_1309x812.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!bS3e!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcd921205-081e-4f13-b590-b3e3b03242bf_1309x812.png\" width=\"1309\" height=\"812\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/cd921205-081e-4f13-b590-b3e3b03242bf_1309x812.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:812,&quot;width&quot;:1309,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:234336,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/189131281?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcd921205-081e-4f13-b590-b3e3b03242bf_1309x812.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!bS3e!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcd921205-081e-4f13-b590-b3e3b03242bf_1309x812.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!bS3e!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcd921205-081e-4f13-b590-b3e3b03242bf_1309x812.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!bS3e!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcd921205-081e-4f13-b590-b3e3b03242bf_1309x812.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!bS3e!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fcd921205-081e-4f13-b590-b3e3b03242bf_1309x812.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">NVO has been on a steady down trend for months. This is also an example of why I despise anonymous “Investor” pages and “buy the dip” accounts. They fight the trend and lead their investors astray, giving a bad reputation to the finance niche. “Invest in Quality” and his followers here, have been fighting the trend for more than a year, <strong>compounding losses</strong>. NVO is down -74%. </figcaption></figure></div><p>Though I like the Russel 2000 more, the S&amp;P 500 is forming higher lows locally. This is a great sign for another run. Just be patient. </p><h4>Recession Resistant Stocks Continue To Demonstrate Strength</h4><p>Several sectors have not even flinched during the pullback. As also mentioned in <em><strong><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/leaders-forming-under-the-surface?r=4z8lgl\">Stock Market Leaders Forming Under the Surface</a></strong></em> , drilling and marine shipping continue to run upwards. The stocks provided in that article, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$FRO&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> , <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$RIG&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> and <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$VAL&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span>  are all up between 7% to 9% since posting. The point being: there are still winners out there, particularly recession assets. </p><p>Personally, I would <strong>avoid tech</strong>. With major names like  <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$MSFT&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> and <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$AMZN&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> showing incredible weakness, these are sector leaders…making it more common for them to drag down smaller names within their own sector. You have no idea if one of those dips becomes the next Novo Nordisk seen above…wait for strength. </p><p><strong>Please Like ❤️ and Restack this post! Only way past the AI slop on substack. </strong></p><p><a href=\"https://substack.com/@stocktok/note/c-219242822?r=4z8lgl&amp;utm_source=notes-share-action&amp;utm_medium=web\">Gold and Silver Are Not Done</a>, its not time to buy, per my strategy…but they are not showing any signs that the larger run is over with. Gold needs to reach $5598+ and silver needs to reach $121+ for me to re-open my <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$PAAS&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> position, a silver miner, we took a +30.6% profit on. An alert will be sent out, when and if I take that position for subscribers. </p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><h4>Now, some updates on my personal positions and plans going forward. </h4>",
